    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d562-a1">

                <pb facs="0793" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg773"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Peck to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Syracuse, New York,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-11-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 10, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>To Secretary <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seward.</hi></p>
                <p>Just from Buffalo. The Georgiana is near Port Colborne, twenty miles distant. She
                    was lately purchased at Toronto, Canada West, for commercial purposes, and
                    seventeen thousand dollars in gold paid. The price is far beyond her value, in
                    the opinion of the best judges. This, in connexion with the fact that the
                    business season is at an end, stamps the transaction with suspicion, and
                    warrants the belief that she is intended for raiding operations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN J. PECK, <hi rendition="#italic">Major
                    General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
